// EXPECT: PASS
// README "Eponymous Naming": "if just a name (no colon) is used, and the
// name is of a[n] Object that's not already a child of this object, and
// the Object is not being re-opened (by { or .), then a new child is
// created having the same name as the supertype." This is the spec's
// own example (Event/Date), adapted to use a locally-declared Date
// Syntax.
//
// "Date" inside "Event: { Date }" is not already a child of Event, but
// is found by ascending to TOP (the same way a supertype name would be
// resolved) - so a new Event child named "Date", with supertype Date,
// gets created: exactly as if "Date: Date;" had been written directly.
// Confirmed by hand (ADL_DEBUG=1) that the resulting tree shows
// `Event : Object { Date : Date; }`.
TOP {
	Date: {
		Syntax = /\d\d\d\d-\d\d-\d\d/
	}
	Event: {
		Date
	}
	: Event { Date = 2001-03-19 }
}
